  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image shows a young child with curly hair holding cotton candy, looking upward with an expression of surprise or delight. The text overlay reads, 'you mean i don't have to pick it and i can eat it?!' The meme humorously depicts the child's innocent and excited reaction to the idea that they don't need to pick up the cotton candy (perhaps implying it's already in their possession or being offered) and can simply eat it. There is no toxicity present in this meme. The intent is purely comedic and lighthearted, using the child's innocent reaction to create humor around the simple pleasure of eating cotton candy. The child's appearance is not being used to stereotype or demean any group, and the content is not harmful, hateful, abusive, cyberbullying, misogynistic, or propagandistic. The meme relies on the contrast between the child's naive excitement and the mundane reality of cotton candy being a treat to be consumed, not picked up.",
